course: dictionary
lesson: 4055
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word «generously» tells you how someone does something. Context clues help you pick the right meaning. In «The wicked borrow and do not repay, but the righteous give generously», the words borrow and repay show that giving generously means giving freely and kindly, not just paying back what is owed.
explain: Generously can also mean in a large amount. «Spread the butter generously» means use plenty, not a thin layer. Always ask: what word would fit here? Try swapping in a meaning, such as a lot or freely, and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Generously can mean kind giving, plenty, or fair and kind when judging others. The rest of the sentence shows you which one the writer means.
fact: Generously is an adverb, so it tells you how something is done: give generously, spread generously.
fact: «Generously» means in a kind way that gives more money, time or help than expected.
fact: «Generously» can also mean in a large amount, as in «generously sized».
fact: «Generously» can mean fair and kind when judging others.
fact: Generous is the root word, and more generously and most generously show the degree.
exercise: «The righteous give generously.» What does give generously mean here? | *Give more than expected, in a kind way | Give in a hurry to get rid of it | Give nothing at all | Give only when someone asks
exercise: «Spread the butter generously on the toast.» What does generously mean here? | Cold | Thinly, so you can barely see it | Quickly and carelessly | *In a large amount, using plenty
exercise: Which word is the root word of generously? | *generous | gene | genuine | general
test: «The teacher judged the runners generously and gave them all a second chance.» What does generously mean here? | *Fair and kind when judging others | Quietly | Unfairly and harshly | In a hurry
test: «Many people gave generously to the appeal.» What does generously mean here? | Did not give at all | *Gave more than expected, in a kind way | Gave by accident | Gave the smallest amount possible
exam: Which word best keeps the meaning of generously in «The righteous give generously»? | Stingily | *Freely and kindly | Greedily | Carelessly
